[281.828761, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m I now have a complete picture. Let me make the design decision and implement a correct, well-scoped slice.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m **Design decision (the spec's explicit ask): completion model = per-commit.** Each stack member is Completed when its *own* commit lands on main — via AIDA's existing `done→completed` auto-bump — not held until the whole stack lands. Rationale: `completed` already *means* \"merged to the default branch\"; once a member's PR merges it genuinely is on main, so withholding the status would misreport tree state, and the atomic model would need a new barrier for zero benefit.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m Let me confirm the implementation approach against the CLI wiring and integrate.rs style before coding.\r\n"]
[282.581145, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m \u001b[36mRead\u001b[0m: /home/joe/ai/aida-pool-aida-0/aida-cli/src/integrate.rs\r\n"]
