[881.103503, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m Done. TASK-841 is complete as an implementer pickup.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m ## Summary\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m **TASK-841 — integrate: stacked-branch accumulation strategy** → Done, PR [#1297](https://github.com/joemooney/aida/pull/1297) open, queue empty.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m The spec explicitly gated on a **design decision before implementing**, so I made and recorded it:\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m ### Decision — completion model = PER-COMMIT\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m Each stacked member is Completed when its **own** commit lands on the default branch (via the existing `done→completed` auto-bump, STORY-86), *not* held until the whole stack lands. `completed` already means \"merged to the default branch,\" so once a member's PR merges it genuinely is on main — an atomic whole-stack barrier would misreport a landed member as still-Done for zero benefit and need new machinery. So the integrator's only extra job over `per-item` is **order + gate** — no completion machinery added.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m ### Implementation (safe, unit-tested slice)\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m - `integrate::plan_stacked_integration` — pure planner (4 tests) splitting the ready set into *mergeable bottom layer* vs *deferred* (stacked behind another still-open branch; merging it now would drag the parent's un-squashed commits in under the wrong PR).\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m - `handle_queue_integrate` — `--strategy stacked` now drives only the mergeable layer, prints a `⏸` line per deferred member, and exits `2` so `--watch`/a wrapping loop re-checks after the layer lands.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m - `strategy_unsupported_message` — `stacked` is no longer a hard \"not built\" error.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m ### Follow-up filed — TASK-1080\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m The forge-mutating piece I deliberately scoped out: force-push a promoted child's PR branch via the stack-aware `git rebase --onto origin/main <parent_sha>` so 2nd+ layers become mergeable automatically instead of deferring with an `/aida-rebase` pointer. (The STORY-248 cascade rebases the child worktree locally on `aida pull` but doesn't force-push the PR branch.)\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m Build + fmt + targeted tests green. I did **not** merge — leaving PR #1297 for CI/review (won't merge red per your gate).\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m One open item from session start: **2 findings await triage** (`aida awaiting`) — untouched, flagging as promised.\r\n"]
[881.357488, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:task-841]\u001b[0m ✓ result 850330ms $4.8450\r\n"]
