[1531.721981, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m Context is now clear. Let me decode it before proceeding:\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m - My session (`019f1c48`, reviewer, PR-1297, in `/home/joe/ai/aida-pr-1297`) is an **interactive** reviewer — 52s old, freshly launched by the user's slash command.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m - `aida zen status` = `interactive` (the corroborated signal).\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m - `AIDA_HEADLESS=1`, `AIDA_REVIEW_VERDICT_FILE` (pointing at `/home/joe/ai/aida/…`, a **different** repo, where the file doesn't even exist), and `orchestrated` are **leaked from the parent environment** — there's no drain.lock or orchestrator state in this repo, and a real orchestrator driving this review would write the verdict file *inside this repo*.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m This is exactly the BUG-237-family hazard the skill warns about: a stale/leaked env var must not silently switch me into headless/orchestrated mode. So I'll treat this as a **standalone interactive review**, pause for you before any merge, and **not** write to that cross-repo verdict file. Now the actual review — let me read the spec, checklist, and full diff.\r\n"]
