[1598.309843, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m The one real correctness risk: if a bottom-of-stack member records `parent_branch` as `origin/main` while `default_short` is `main`, the planner would wrongly **defer** it (`entry.parent_branch == default_branch` fails). Let me verify the form `lease.parent_branch` takes at fork time.\r\n"]
[1601.311904, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m \u001b[36mBash\u001b[0m: cd /home/joe/ai/aida-pr-1297 echo \"=== where lease.parent_branch is SET (session_start / worktree create) ===\" grep -rn …\r\n"]
[1605.566484, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m \u001b[36mBash\u001b[0m: cd /home/joe/ai/aida-pr-1297 echo \"=== stack_parent_branch computation (52225-52270) ===\" sed -n '52225,52270p' aida-cli…\r\n"]
[1622.839093, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m Confirmed the critical invariant: `stack_parent_branch` at fork time strips `origin/` (line 52234: `.strip_prefix(\"origin/\")`), and `default_short` in the planner strips it identically. Both sides use the short form (`main`), and the existing cascade filter (line 103572) uses the same comparison. **No origin/-prefix mismatch bug** — a bottom-of-stack member forked from main records `parent_branch = \"main\"` and is correctly classified mergeable.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m Now let me run the focused test plan. CI is already green (Build ubuntu-latest passed 8m22s), but I'll verify the planner tests directly.\r\n"]
