[1820.537681, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m Review complete. Here's the verdict — pausing for your merge decision.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m ## Review: PR-1297 — `feat(integrate): stacked-branch accumulation strategy (TASK-841)`\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m | Spec | Verdict | Evidence |\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m |------|---------|----------|\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m | **TASK-841** | ✅ **PASS** | Design gate decided + implemented + tested; CI green |\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m **What it does.** TASK-841 was a \"decide the completion model, then build it\" task. The PR decides **per-commit completion** (each stacked member Completed when its own commit lands via STORY-86 auto-bump — no whole-stack barrier, since `completed` already means merged-to-main) and implements `--strategy stacked` as a pure stack-aware ordering/gating layer over the existing per-item drive.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m **Verification I ran:**\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m - 4 planner unit tests (`plan_stacked_*`) — green\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m - 2 changed strategy-support tests — green\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m - CI Build (ubuntu-latest) — ✅ PASS 8m22s; PR is `CLEAN` / `MERGEABLE`\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m **Adversarial deep-pass — one real risk checked and cleared:** the planner compares `entry.parent_branch == default_branch`. I traced the fork-time recording (`main.rs:52234`) — `parent_branch` is stored with `origin/` **stripped**, and the planner's `default_short` strips it identically (matching the existing cascade filter at `103572`). So a bottom-of-stack branch forked from main records `\"main\"` and is correctly classified mergeable — **no prefix-mismatch that would wrongly defer everything.**\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m **One non-blocking observation** (already tracked as **TASK-1080**): a member whose stack-parent already merged but whose branch isn't yet rebased is *deferred* with a `/aida-rebase`-then-re-run pointer rather than auto-promoted. That's the honest slice boundary — safe (defers rather than mis-merges).\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]"]
[1820.537727, "o", "\u001b[0m Consolidated review comment posted: https://github.com/joemooney/aida/pull/1297#issuecomment-4850785583\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m ---\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m ⚠️ **One thing to flag before I do anything irreversible.** This session's environment has `AIDA_HEADLESS=1`, `orchestrated`, and `AIDA_REVIEW_VERDICT_FILE=/home/joe/ai/aida/.aida/review-verdicts/PR-1297.json` set — but that path is in a **different repo** than my worktree (`/home/joe/ai/aida-pr-1297`), the file doesn't exist there, and there's no drain.lock/orchestrator state in *this* repo. `aida zen status` reports `interactive`. So I've treated these as **leaked parent-env vars**, not a live orchestrator, and deliberately did **not** write to that cross-repo verdict file or touch any sentinel. If you *did* intend an orchestrated drain to be driving this, let me know and I'll reconcile — otherwise this is a normal interactive review.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:pr-1297]\u001b[0m **Verdict is Approved (own-PR, so no formal `gh pr review --approve`).** Shall I `gh pr merge 1297 --squash --delete-branch`? After merge I'll `aida pull` to auto-bump TASK-841 Done → Completed and close out review STORY-748.\r\n"]
